From a6181328645d1fd86da76b216b0ca7f86a61be82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stsiakal <spiros.tsiakalos1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:10:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tools: add a read-only per-frame call trace to the client
 driver

The movement recon needs to know which x2game actor-update functions run per frame for the local player. calls.tsv only shows direct calls, so the disassembly cannot answer for virtual slots.

The driver now takes a 'K' trace request. It patches each requested x2game entry with a thunk that saves flags/registers, increments an in-DLL counter, records (function, ECX) and replays the original prologue before jumping back. A frame row is flushed at the System script-system Update; the prologue relocation refuses unknown encodings. Nothing in game state is written.

- native/trace.{h,cpp}: detour generator, frame rows, dump/clear/install/uninstall/selftest.
- native/trace-test.cpp + build.bat: stand-alone selftest on synthetic prologues (short mov and SEH entries), run by the native build.
- native/aadriver.cpp: route K requests on the main thread and flush one row from the System Update hook.

Deliberately unchanged: no game state writes, no vtable hacks, no anti-cheat interaction, the player build and all existing pipe operations.
